WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.210
<i>I'm in great shape today.</i>

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:06.480
<i>I beat my time up the rear 
gate slope by ten seconds.</i>

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:12.280
<i>I won the Minegayama race the 
other day, Makishima-san.</i>

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.850
What's up, Onoda-kun? You writing a letter?

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:23.280
To a girl?

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.380
N-No, it's a report.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.870
It's for my math homework.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.630
Sucks for you. That's a lot of pages.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.270
Will you even be able to pass this year?

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:33.060
What?!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.720
<b>Sohoku
High
School
Bicycle
Racing
Club</b>

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.930
<i>I don't know his address, though.</i>

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.410
Finished your homework?

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.060
Teshima-san...

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.570
Don't get your hopes up.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.050
He hardly ever writes back.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.030
Even if you pour your concerns 
out to him, he just says, "Yeah."

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.990
It's Makishima-san's address.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.000
What?

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.000
I got it from Pierre-sensei.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.250
Now you'll be able to solve 
lots of math problems.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:11.630
Yes, sir.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:16.010
Things change over time.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:20.430
Until now, you've only needed 
to listen to your seniors.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.180
But going forward, you'll have 
to use your own judgment.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.810
The first-years will be joining soon.

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.560
We'll race in the Inter-High again.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:35.030
As you lead those first-years, you'll have 
to decide your own path for yourself.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.030
If you're ever unsure, do this.

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:46.120
Consider all your options, and pick 
the first one that comes to mind.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.710
<b>Chiba</b>

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.710
<b>Kanagawa</b>

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:51.340
<i>Teshima-san's racing in the mountains...</i>

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:53.590
<i>On Irohazaka!</i>

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.320
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:28.770
<i>RIDE.23  Sakamichi's Pursuit</i>

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.770
<i>Teshima-san's racing up Irohazaka.</i>

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.520
Irohazaka will be difficult.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.130
It'll be the turning point.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.860
Each team will be sending their ace climber.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:40.900
<i>His only orders were to keep toward 
the front and stay with the team.</i>

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.610
<i>But that can't be right.</i>

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.660
<i>His message probably the same 
as during the Minegayama race.</i>

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.950
<i>"I'll be waiting for you in 
the mountains. Follow me."</i>

00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:00.460
<i>Number 1's pressure changed 
the moment he saw the sign.</i>

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:01.500
<i>Watch out.</i>

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.470
<i>He's going to make his move.</i>

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:03.740
<i>We know.</i>

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.120
<i>He's not getting anywhere.</i>

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.470
<i>He'll definitely try to surprise us.</i>

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.810
Excuse me. I'm going to pass you now!

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:12.010
A direct...

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.230
...declaration of war?

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.150
Princess!

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.650
"Princess"? What's that?

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.100
I've heard of this!

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.540
When Sohoku High School's 
Onoda starts singing to himself...

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.200
He gets faster!

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:28.220
I've always kept these feelings secret!

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.200
Be my princess forever, ta-tum-tum-tum!

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.710
Just block him!

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.290
The anime I most highly
recommend, <i>Love Hime</i>,

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.590
ended its first season 
amidst great popularity.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.780
After taking a break in September,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.540
the long-awaited second season 
started the other day.

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:44.700
First? First what?

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.020
Does he think he can place first?

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:46.940
You won't pass us.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:49.390
"The Princess's Spinning One-Sided Love"
is the powered-up

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:54.520
second season opening theme of
<i>Love Hime Pettanko</i>, which is back on the air!

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:59.030
Opening? What's back?

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.770
I have no idea what he's talking about!

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.810
Princess!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:08.190
I've always kept these feelings secret!

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.430
What on earth is he?

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.490
Don't shrink from him! There's three of us!

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.780
Be my princess forever!

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:16.500
I've always kept these feelings secret!

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:18.130
He's smiling! Can he go even faster?

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.140
Be my princess forever!

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.400
Princess! Spin, spin, spin!

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.950
He passed us!

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.720
Miracle, spin, spin, spin! Ah, ah, ah!

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.720
A miracle?

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.550
But we slowed him down for five minutes.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.580
He can't catch up to the front now.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:30.970
I'm not so sure.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:37.230
While we were keeping him at a slow pace, 
he may have been saving his strength.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:42.430
It's possible his dramatic 
pursuit is about to begin...

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:47.110
<i>Turn! Turn, legs!</i>

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.900
Princess!

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:50.990
We're going uphill!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:52.290
"Princess"?

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.540
What was Sohoku High School's 
#1 doing behind us?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.750
<i>Teshima-san, I'm coming.</i>

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.570
What do you mean, "dramatic pursuit"?

00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:04.550
He means to catch up to the front.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.640
That's impossible.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:06.880
We slowed him down for so long.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.930
And the pack's ahead of him.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.930
It's impossible for him to 
race for the mountain results.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.390
When I cut in front of him,

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.690
instead of reflexively dodging me
or braking like normal,

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:22.400
he just kept staring off into the distance.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.990
Like his goal was far ahead of him.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:34.760
I've always kept these feelings secret!

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.660
#1's coming!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.220
Sohoku High School second-year 
Onoda Sakamichi!

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.410
Did he break through the barricade?

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.660
Be my princess forever, ta-tum-tum-tum!

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.000
Princess! Spin, spin, spin!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.380
It's Sohoku High School's 
Onoda's Singing Climb!

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.680
Miracle, spin, spin, spin! Ah, ah, ah!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.160
Don't let him through! Block the road!

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:45.980
Yes, sir!

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:46.910
Don't bother.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.020
Yamagiwa-san...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.470
Road racing is a gentleman's sport.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:56.560
Last year's champion 
deserves the most respect.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:00.270
We didn't even send a climber 
to compete for the mountains.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:05.940
Blocking him for no strategic 
reason would be uncool.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:11.660
This is the respect we have for tag #1.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.290
Thank you!

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.790
Thanks for the help.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.540
Excuse me.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:21.790
His hips are so low.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.380
That's #1...

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.890
I would've bragged like 
crazy if I took #1.

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:28.880
He's our opponent, but he's still amazing.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.220
He makes me want to cheer for him.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.930
It's tag #1!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.720
The pack's right in front of you!

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.100
Once you pass that, your team's right there!

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.310
Princess!

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.690
<i>I can almost see the pack.</i>

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.270
<i>Once I pass that, I'll be with my team.</i>

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.750
Excuse me. Let me through, please!

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.180
Thank you!

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:58.690
You think he'll make it all the way there?

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:00.580
It's not that simple.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:04.500
Road racing is aiming for victory as a team.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.790
Naturally, there will be some 
who won't want to let him pass.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.300
<i>I made it through the pack.</i>

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:19.850
Kyoto Fushimi High School...

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:30.690
What's wrong? You look 
like you've seen a ghost.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.390
Midousuji-kun...

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:42.660
<i>Midousuji-kun again...</i>

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:44.740
You in a hurry?

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:49.050
Lose something important?

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:57.260
Something similar happened 
last year, didn't it?

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:02.130
What did you lose?

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:06.600
Sorry, but I'm controlling this pack.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:10.310
<i>I need to get past Midousuji-kun.</i>

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:11.570
<i>Through Kyoto Fushimi High School.</i>

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.240
Komori-kun...

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:24.260
You must've lost something 
irreplaceable to you.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.750
Was it your trust? Your role?

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:28.840
Your eyes are desperate.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:31.160
<i>I need to get back to the others.</i>

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.750
<i>To Teshima-san!</i>

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:38.140
But whatever you've lost isn't coming back.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.010
Let me through!

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.160
You're not getting through, #1.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.610
As Kyoto Fushimi High School's 
captain and secret ace,

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:54.550
and as a rider must stronger than I was
last year, I, Mizuta Nobuyuki, will stop you.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:58.780
I'm the guy who stopped Hakone Academy
High School's #2, Arakita Yasutomo.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.870
I am Kyoto Fushimi High School's Iron Wall!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:03.290
Mizuta-kun!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:07.320
All I did was instruct you to enter Phase 9.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:10.330
Stop #1 if he tries to get ahead.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.170
I didn't say you could chat with him.

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.340
<i>Midousuji-kun looked bigger for a second.</i>

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.970
I-I'm not.

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.680
As the team's captain, I was 
just telling him who we are.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:25.530
We don't need that kind of vanity.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:32.350
What my team needs is
perfect soldiers. True Zakus.

00:10:32.350 --> 00:10:35.940
With only the will to move forward, 
even if their arms and legs fall off.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:40.290
If you're going to show off your 
individuality just because it's the Inter-High,

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:41.620
I'll let you go...

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.120
At any time.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:49.460
I-I get it, Midousuji-kun.

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:51.700
<i>Midousuji...</i>

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:56.210
We have only one goal this year.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.220
And that's victory.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:01.920
<i>He seems bigger lately.</i>

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.890
<i>That pressure...</i>

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:10.440
Anyone thinking too many stupid 
thoughts to keep up can quit.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.650
<i>Eighty percent of the first-years
who joined this year quit.</i>

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:18.000
<b>Kyoto Fushimi High School
Graduation</b>

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.490
There you are, Ishigaki-san.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.680
I graduated.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.580
I need to thank you, Yama.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.840
Thanks for your help.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:30.660
Oh, no. Thank you.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.630
You worked hard at the Inter-High.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:38.010
I remember how you pulled on the 
flats during the second day.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.320
It was amazing.

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:42.180
I dropped out in the mountains 
after that, though.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:45.110
I'm counting on you to 
carry the team next year.

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:45.760
What?

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:49.640
You should be telling 
Mizuta and Midousuji that.

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:52.600
I'll just be doing my 
best as their assistant.

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.770
Everyone's waiting.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.320
Let's go to the third-year sendoff party.

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:00.070
Midousuji won't be there, though.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:00.850
Yama...

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.410
You're a patient guy.

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:07.540
What?

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.440
Midousuji is a talented rider.

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.710
His legs are strong,
and his instincts are good.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.330
He has leadership qualities, too.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.560
But to win at road races,

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:21.110
in the end, you need a conscience to 
tell you to believe in each other.

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:26.600
Yama, you have to be Midousuji's conscience.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:27.780
What?

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:30.850
When the time comes, the one 
who stops Midousuji will be...

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:33.600
<i>...you, Yama.</i>

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.650
<i>You want me to stop Midousuji?</i>

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:37.940
<i>Can I do that?</i>

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.460
I know this guy can be trouble, too.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:49.830
After all, he took the final peak last year.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:53.870
It's been a while, Sakamichi.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.210
Midousuji-kun...

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.420
Let me through!

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.270
Let you through?

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:06.730
Do you want to go? No matter what?

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:07.930
In that case...

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.430
Shall we work together?

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:12.560
Work together?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:16.980
You really think you'll make it to the 
front when you're this far behind?

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:21.350
Even if you did catch up, you'd be exhausted.

00:13:21.350 --> 00:13:23.690
You might not be able to accomplish anything.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:29.660
But if you and I ride together,

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:33.060
we'll be half as tired.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:38.750
I know. I'll send Yamaguchi-kun, too.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.000
We'll have him pedal, too.

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:45.340
Then we'll be one-third as tired.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:49.410
I want to go to the front. So do you.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.110
Our goals are aligned.

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:54.620
What could be more convenient?

00:13:54.620 --> 00:13:57.690
<i>I thought he would try to stop me.</i>

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.020
Come on.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:05.280
We fought each other last year.

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:09.030
There's no need to hold back.
I'll pull first.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:13.830
Why are you thinking? Don't think so much.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.910
Anyone would take the faster 
train to get to their destination,

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:20.380
if the express and regular 
trains cost the same.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:22.750
You're supposed to say yes.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.630
It's simple.

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:28.850
<i>What will happen if I go with Midousuji-kun?</i>

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:31.280
<i>I'll get there faster, but is that all?</i>

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:35.170
<i>Think, think. Um...</i>

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:38.120
<i>Let's go together.</i>

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:40.830
<i>Take me to the front,</i>

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:45.150
<i>and you can fight for the mountain 
result to your heart's content.</i>

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.930
<i>I'll be cheering for you.</i>

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:52.910
<i>But after that, I'll be 
taking the finish line.</i>

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:56.110
Hurry up. The train's leaving.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:57.560
Beeeeep.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.250
<i>Think, think...</i>

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:02.410
Please hurry if you're boarding the train.

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:04.480
Tweedle, tweedle, tweedle...

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.880
<i>Think, think.</i>

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:09.510
You'll have to decide your 
own path for yourself.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.180
If you're ever unsure, do this.

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:20.100
Consider all your options, and pick 
the first one that comes to mind.

00:15:20.710 --> 00:15:23.160
Sorry, but I'll pass.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:24.940
I'll reach the front on my own.

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:28.570
Sorry for rejecting your offer, Midousuji-kun!

00:15:29.270 --> 00:15:32.610
<i>He said no under these circumstances.</i>

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:34.180
Huh...

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:36.240
<i>Apparently, he's not an idiot.</i>

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.370
So let me through!

00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:45.630
I can't do that, but if you can 
break away from him, you can go.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.220
Yamaguchi-kun.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:50.980
What?

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.090
You're up.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.930
This guy...

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.220
I just have to break away from this guy.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:02.500
You can handle Phase 11, can't you?

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:04.600
Go stop #1.

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:05.900
What?

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:08.320
You're not sending me, Midousuji-kun?

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:14.850
You can do it if you throw away the 
unnecessary things you're dearly holding onto.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:18.850
<i>You have to be Midousuji's conscience.</i>

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:24.130
Princess!

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:25.040
Hurry up, Yamaguchi-kun.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:30.380
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:37.660
Why am I chasing after #1 in the mountains?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:38.810
I'm...

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:42.730
I'm a sprinter, Midousuji.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:46.860
Be his conscience.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:50.700
Why does everyone always make 
such unreasonable demands of me?

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:54.680
<i>I can't do it.</i>

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:57.160
<i>I just used up all my strength.</i>

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:01.790
<i>I can't stop him. I...</i>

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.640
Are you a first-year?

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:05.920
Still deciding which club to join?

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.830
Yeah. I used to play basketball,

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:10.920
but I thought I'd do something 
different in high school.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:12.910
Why don't you try biking?

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:16.090
We've got a good team,
and we win regularly in Kyoto.

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:18.800
I can't join a club that's too strong.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:22.520
I could never be the best, and I don't 
like being the center of attention.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:26.140
Bike riding is a team sport.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:28.520
It's a sport of people who 
work behind the scenes.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:31.380
<i>A team sport...</i>

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:35.790
That's it. Hold that position.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:36.450
Yes, sir.

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:39.350
Hold that position until you 
make it through the corner.

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:40.410
Yes, sir.

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:42.560
Thanks, Yama.

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.570
Thanks to you, I won.

00:17:44.570 --> 00:17:46.160
Yes, sir.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:50.190
<i>I thought I was happy living in the shadows.</i>

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:54.590
<i>Honestly, I was uncertain when I was 
chosen to be on the Inter-High team.</i>

00:17:55.560 --> 00:18:02.140
<i>I can't handle fighting on the 
front lines of the Inter-High.</i>

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.450
Wa...

00:18:13.930 --> 00:18:15.900
Wait!

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.950
<i>How did he reject Midousuji like that?</i>

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:28.870
<i>He seems like a pushover. He's so small.</i>

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.550
<i>How can he climb like that?</i>

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:35.690
<i>He smells like a man of the shadows, like me.</i>

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:37.930
<i>Is he not?</i>

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.140
Who waits when their opponents 
tell them to wait?

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.890
<i>Onoda must be a good guy.</i>

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:52.650
You were right to reject Midousuji's offer.

00:18:53.320 --> 00:19:00.090
If you'd worked together with Midousuji, 
Sohoku High School would've lost.

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:02.120
Really?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:04.370
You have good instincts.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:07.820
Th-Thank you, um...

00:19:07.820 --> 00:19:09.000
I'm a third-year, Yama.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:11.620
Yama-san...

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:13.710
Excuse me!

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:18.010
<i>What a strange guy.</i>

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:21.230
<i>"He has a strange aura about him."</i>

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.690
<i>Ishigaki-san said the same thing.</i>

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:26.950
<i>An aura different from Midousuji's.</i>

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.320
Onoda-san!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.110
Sorry I'm late!

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:40.950
You idiot! How long were 
you gonna make us wait?

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:42.860
Sorry.

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:45.910
You made it through that 
pack? That's amazing.

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:49.200
Good work catching up. Rest in the back.

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.670
Um, I-I...

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:55.040
Touichirou...

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:57.660
Trouble caught up.

00:19:57.660 --> 00:19:59.450
Want me to keep him in check?

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:00.720
No, don't bother.

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:03.740
There's no need to waste our energy.

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.660
I'm directing the team right now.

00:20:09.110 --> 00:20:11.270
This is what Teshima-san told us.

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:15.190
If Onoda makes it through the 
blockade and catches up to the team,

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.610
send him to the front if he's less 
than three and a half minutes behind.

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:21.470
Onoda's strong enough to 
catch up to the front.

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.360
But if it's more than that...

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:27.200
You can't catch up to the front.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:30.890
It's already been four and 
a half. It's been too long.

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:32.730
Imaizumi-kun...

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:36.840
No matter how hard you pedal, you may not 
even catch a glimpse of Teshima-san's back.

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:40.030
It's smarter for you to rest 
your legs with the team.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:43.590
Do you still want to go?

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:45.700
Yeah.

00:20:46.840 --> 00:20:49.510
Sheesh. You're unbelievable.

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:51.140
Sorry.

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.560
Take this.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:57.860
When Teshima-san left, he left 
one behind to lighten his load.

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.970
He's probably parched.

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.430
Tell him we're rooting for him.

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:05.330
Onoda...

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:07.950
Junta is fighting.

00:21:09.230 --> 00:21:10.680
Take our hopes.

00:21:13.820 --> 00:21:17.290
Take them to him, Sakamichi!

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:18.920
Yes, sir!

00:22:54.710 --> 00:22:56.560
I'm going to be late.

00:22:56.560 --> 00:22:59.900
Unbelievable. You're a 
second-year starting today.

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:02.880
You haven't matured at all, Kotori-sama.

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:04.200
Yeah, but...

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:07.010
When I think about seeing 
Arimaru-kun again...

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:14.390
You're as defenseless as ever, Kotori.

00:23:14.390 --> 00:23:15.410
Sheesh.

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:17.610
You're so mean, Kotaro-kun.

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:20.870
I'll take care of you from now on.

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:26.500
<i>Why is my heart pounding?</i>

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:28.690
<i>I've always kept (spin, spin)</i>

00:23:28.690 --> 00:23:31.330
<i>These feelings secret (spin, spin)</i>

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:34.140
<i>Be my princess forever (ta-tum-tum-tum)</i>

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:35.910
What?

00:23:36.200 --> 00:23:39.890
<i>NEXT RIDE  The Ride of Weeds</i>

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:44.900
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.
